      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "If $∠C$ and $∠D$ are complementary angles and $m∠C={51}^{∘}$, find the measure of $∠D.$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14186058/assets/a910150e8bcfe1d8b4d5e16dd2244a4f5e4da7d6ad965b606293128f8595fa09.png)\n\nSince $∠C$ and $∠D$ are complementary, the sum of their measures is equal to ${90}^{∘}.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠C+m∠D & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ {51}^{∘}+m∠D & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ m∠D & ={39}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
